id: mem-e8d2c803
name: No hanging words in text
description: >-
  Avoid orphan/widow words that wrap onto a line by themselves in headlines and body text



  Avoid hanging words — single words that wrap onto their own line in headlines, subtitles, or body
  text. Use `&nbsp;` between short word pairs (e.g., "AI&nbsp;agents", "can&nbsp;read") to keep them
  together.


  **Why:** It looks unpolished and breaks visual rhythm, especially on large hero text.


  **How to apply:** When writing any marketing/hero/headline text on the site, check for orphans at
  common viewport widths. Use non-breaking spaces (`&nbsp;` in JSX) to glue short word pairs
  together.
category: documentation
trigger: postflight
severity: advisory
check:
  type: context-checked
  params: {}
enabled: false
